e kind, and nothing to K1 or K4. Section 4.3 gives the sentences that promises 1, 7 and 11 gain in LV5. The promises do not change in this head. If you refuse the exception, the level waits.\n\nOther paths: docs/kernel.md gains one paragraph in section 7 and one item in 7.1. The volatile acts note gains a pointer at the head of section 16, and 16.1 reads \"Live, Recorded or Sequenced\". The sequenced note's sections 2 and 3 say that a live scope keeps no entry after its creation.\n\nSources. A read-only agent wrote the brief at ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-10-planner-briefs/live-level-brief.md, with each fact marked as read or inferred. I read these myself at main: `confirmation` in packages/derive/src/delivery.ts (the confirmation is an entry that activates the scope), `Entry` and `Input` in packages/contract/src/entry.ts, `validateFormat1`, `judgeAct`'s accepted-intent index in packages/derive/src/judge.ts, and docs/kernel.md sections 2 and 5 to 7.1.\n\nNot verified, stated as design: that the judges of derive run over a memory state with no sealed entry and no change (LV2 says what it must change, and any change there is kernel), what a live scope answers to a late delivery (O2), and the bound on live state (O1).\n\nChecks: scripts/check-notes.mjs against main reports 0 warnings. The link checker reports 1228 local links, 0 broken. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no gate.","body":{"commit":"56c7b8ed07f9692ab2b72574dedba4487425945e","path":"notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md"}}